# Kite Weather
#
# A warm, faded afternoon heard through a worn cassette. No drums.
#
# Everything plays through the same tired tape: heavy wow, hiss, dulled
# highs, pads of two slightly detuned oscillators through the Juno chorus.
# The harmony is major and a little sad — Dmaj9, F#m7, Gmaj9, then the turn
# to G minor with a sixth that makes the whole thing ache — and the tune is
# simple enough to have been hummed, sitting low, sliding between notes.
#
#   bars 1-8    pad, a soft bass floor, a few distant plucks
#   bars 9-16   the tune
#   bars 17-24  the tune answers higher; the plucks fill in; the pad opens;
#               at bar 20 the tape sags and every voice sags with it
#   bars 25-28  thinning out, and the tape slows to a stop
#
# 4/4 at 88 bpm; bar n starts at beat 4*(n-1).

bpm 88
gate 0.95
tail 4

# --- the tape everything lives on
automate tape_wow
0.42 R:76 0.6:2@smooth 0.42:4@smooth R:26 0.55:4@smooth
automate tape_flutter
0.1
automate tape_age
0.5
automate tape_drive
0.35
automate chorus_mode
2
automate chorus_rate
0.5
automate chorus_depth
0.45
automate chorus_hiss
0.6
automate spring
0.05
automate reverb_wet
0.3
automate reverb_decay
0.78
automate reverb_tone
3000
automate width
1.1
automate fuzz
0

# A light parallel squeeze, the way a whole cassette dub sits together.
automate comp_in
1
automate comp_threshold
-28
automate comp_ratio
0
automate comp_attack
4
automate comp_release
4
automate comp_makeup
2
automate comp_mix
0.4

# --- pad: Kaini, two saws a few cents apart, slow in and slow out
track pad vel=0.5 patch=kaini reverb_send=0.3
([D3 F#3 A3 C#4 E4]:8 [F#3 A3 C#4 E4]:8 [G3 B3 D4 F#4 A4]:8 [G3 Bb3 D4 E4]:8)x3
[D3 F#3 A3 C#4 E4]:16

# the pad breathes in over the first eight bars and back out at the end
automate pad.gain
0.2 0.6:32@smooth R:64 0.38:16@smooth
automate pad.attack
1.4
automate pad.release
2.5
automate pad.osc2_level
0.6
automate pad.detune
11
automate pad.cutoff
600 R:64 1000:16@smooth R:16 520:16@smooth

# --- bass: Kaini, mono, a sub underneath, roots held long
track bass vel=0.55 patch=kaini gain=0.8
# the floor arrives at bar 5, once the pad has breathed in
R:16 G2:8 G2:8
(D2:8 F#2:8 G2:8 G2:8)x2
D2:16

automate bass.mono
1
automate bass.sub
0.45
automate bass.attack
0.3
automate bass.release
1.5
automate bass.cutoff
380

# --- plucks: Bocuma, a distant music box that never quite rings — played
# by hand: every note a few ms early or late and a touch softer or harder
track pluck vel=0.3 len=0.5 patch=bocuma pan=-0.35 reverb_send=0.4
# 1-8: a few notes on the beat
(D3@0.27~+0.009 R E4@0.25~+0.001 R C#4@0.28~+0.011 R A3@0.24~+0.003 R D3@0.32~+0.014 R E4@0.26~+0.014 R C#4@0.32~-0.004 R A3@0.20~-0.016 R F#3@0.31~-0.007 R E4@0.28~+0.002 R C#4@0.27~-0.004 R A3@0.21~+0.008 R F#3@0.29~+0.019 R E4@0.28~-0.017 R C#4@0.28~-0.002 R A3@0.20~-0.021 R G3@0.29~-0.020 R F#4@0.23~+0.002 R D4@0.31~-0.012 R A3@0.20~-0.004 R G3@0.32~+0.001 R F#4@0.24~-0.005 R D4@0.27~+0.016 R A3@0.22~-0.030 R G3@0.33~-0.003 R E4@0.25~+0.023 R D4@0.33~+0.006 R Bb3@0.25~+0.001 R G3@0.32~+0.012 R E4@0.26~+0.011 R D4@0.28~+0.017 R Bb3@0.22~-0.000 R)
# 9-16: the same, while the tune sings
(D3@0.29~+0.000 R E4@0.22~-0.007 R C#4@0.28~-0.008 R A3@0.25~-0.010 R D3@0.32~-0.012 R E4@0.25~+0.028 R C#4@0.33~+0.011 R A3@0.21~-0.007 R F#3@0.33~+0.006 R E4@0.26~+0.011 R C#4@0.32~+0.010 R A3@0.22~-0.000 R F#3@0.28~-0.016 R E4@0.22~+0.002 R C#4@0.30~-0.001 R A3@0.22~+0.015 R G3@0.30~+0.011 R F#4@0.24~-0.005 R D4@0.31~+0.017 R A3@0.22~+0.012 R G3@0.31~-0.001 R F#4@0.23~+0.002 R D4@0.29~+0.005 R A3@0.22~-0.016 R G3@0.30~+0.012 R E4@0.28~-0.004 R D4@0.29~-0.030 R Bb3@0.25~-0.003 R G3@0.29~-0.010 R E4@0.27~+0.012 R D4@0.33~-0.006 R Bb3@0.24~+0.002 R)
# 17-24: filling in to eighths
(D3@0.31~+0.013 A3@0.31~-0.023 E4@0.28~+0.006 F#4@0.32~-0.011 C#4@0.32~+0.004 A3@0.28~+0.000 E4@0.27~-0.007 A3@0.28~+0.007 D3@0.32~-0.003 A3@0.27~-0.016 E4@0.27~-0.030 F#4@0.32~-0.013 C#4@0.29~-0.013 A3@0.27~-0.006 E4@0.29~+0.003 A3@0.33~-0.015 F#3@0.37~-0.019 C#4@0.31~+0.015 E4@0.31~+0.006 A4@0.31~-0.001 E4@0.27~+0.013 C#4@0.27~-0.010 A3@0.31~-0.021 E4@0.32~-0.004 F#3@0.34~-0.010 C#4@0.32~-0.009 E4@0.28~+0.003 A4@0.29~+0.000 E4@0.32~+0.004 C#4@0.28~+0.012 A3@0.30~+0.004 E4@0.29~-0.002 G3@0.35~+0.010 D4@0.27~-0.014 F#4@0.33~+0.005 A4@0.32~-0.026 B3@0.31~-0.012 D4@0.32~+0.000 A4@0.28~+0.000 F#4@0.28~-0.006 G3@0.37~-0.017 D4@0.31~-0.002 F#4@0.30~-0.013 A4@0.27~-0.003 B3@0.31~+0.012 D4@0.31~-0.002 A4@0.31~+0.021 F#4@0.30~+0.002 G3@0.37~-0.024 D4@0.28~+0.006 E4@0.33~-0.002 Bb3@0.33~+0.024 D4@0.28~+0.005 E4@0.32~-0.006 G4@0.33~-0.000 D4@0.33~+0.010 G3@0.36~+0.024 D4@0.32~+0.000 E4@0.33~+0.002 Bb3@0.31~-0.005 D4@0.31~-0.002 E4@0.28~-0.005 G4@0.27~-0.023 D4@0.30~+0.002)
# 25-28: a few last notes
D3@0.25~+0.018 R R R E4@0.18~-0.006 R R R R R C#4@0.19~-0.002 R R R R R
R R A3@0.17~-0.005 R R R R R R R R R R R R R

automate pluck.vel_filter
1.4

# --- the tune: Kaini B, mono, low, sliding
track tune vel=0.55 patch=kaini-b gain=1.8 reverb_send=0.22
>32
# 9-16
A4:1.5 F#4:0.5 E4:1 D4:1 E4:3 R:1
F#4:1.5 A4:0.5 E4:2 C#4:3 R:1
B3:1 D4:1 F#4:1.5 E4:0.5 D4:3 R:1
Bb3:1.5 D4:0.5 E4:2 D4:3 R:1
# 17-24: the answer, a little higher
F#4:1.5@0.6 A4:0.5@0.6 B4:1@0.65 A4:1@0.6 F#4:3@0.6 R:1
E4:1.5@0.6 F#4:0.5 A4:2@0.65 E4:3@0.6 R:1
D4:1 F#4:1 A4:1.5@0.55 G4:0.5 F#4:3@0.6 R:1
G4:1.5@0.6 Bb4:0.5@0.65 A4:2@0.65 D4:4@0.55
# 25-28
A4:2@0.45 F#4:2@0.42 E4:4@0.4 D4:8@0.38

automate tune.glide
0.11
automate tune.lfo_rate
4.6
automate tune.lfo_pitch
5

# --- the tape sags at bar 20 and every voice sags with it; at the end it
# slows to a stop. One curve, laid on each track.
automate pad.pitch_shift
0 R:76 -0.6:0.75@smooth 0:1.25@smooth R:30 -3:4@smooth
automate bass.pitch_shift
0 R:76 -0.6:0.75@smooth 0:1.25@smooth R:30 -3:4@smooth
automate pluck.pitch_shift
0 R:76 -0.6:0.75@smooth 0:1.25@smooth R:30 -3:4@smooth
automate tune.pitch_shift
0 R:76 -0.6:0.75@smooth 0:1.25@smooth R:30 -3:4@smooth
